title: The Florida Vigilantes
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> officials are murdered in a campaign of political terror.
tags: event
new-page: true
view-if: FL_admitted = 1 and FL_garrison_troops < 8 and FL_kkk_strength + FL_whiteL_strength >= 60
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) + 4;
    Q.kkk_strength += 1;
    Q.FL_freemen_rep -= 2;
    Q.FL_rural_dem += 2;
!}

= The Regulators

Reports from Florida's Panhandle describe a campaign of murder against <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> officials and their supporters. Armed bands calling themselves {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The term draws inspiration from the colonial regulator movement of the 1770s in the Carolinas, where frontier citizens combatted corrupt government officials and outlaws, and formal law enforcement didn't exist">!}**Regulators**{!</span>!} have been riding through the county at night, targeting men known to support the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> government. Their victims appear to have been selected in advance.

The violence began after a local murder that white <span style="color: #0015bc;">**Democrats**</span> blamed on <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span>. Since then, a merchant who sold firearms to freedmen has been killed, along with numerous Black residents. The sheriff has made no serious effort to investigate the killings, and local juries have refused to convict suspected assailants. The state government has been unable to establish effective control over the county.

The remaining <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> officials have received threats against their lives. The circuit clerk, the last white <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> officeholder in the county, is among those marked for death. So is the Black legislator responsible for organizing <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> voters and bringing them to the polls.

Federal troops are scarce in the region. The Regulators appear well aware of their numbers and positions, and the threatened officials have little protection beyond what the government can provide.

[? if FL_occupation_posture >= 1 : Florida has [+ FL_garrison_troops +] thousand federal troops, but none are stationed near the threatened officials. ?][? if FL_occupation_posture < 1 : No federal troops are available in Florida to protect the threatened officials. ?]

- @guard_clerk: Post troops to protect the circuit clerk
- @guard_organizers: Protect the legislator and his organizers
- @warn_leave: Advise both men to leave the county

@guard_clerk
choose-if: army_strength >= 5 and occupation >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if occupation < 1 : We have no authority to station troops there. ?][? if army_strength < 5 : We have no troops to spare. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_occupation_posture = Math.max(1, Q.FL_occupation_posture || 0);
    Q.FL_garrison_troops = (Q.FL_garrison_troops || 0) + 3;
    Q.army_strength -= 3;
    Q.South_army_strength += 3;
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = Math.max(0, (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) - 4);
    Q.FL_middle_class_rep += 2;
    Q.FL_freemen_rep -= 2;
    Q.Union_League_strength = Math.max(0, Q.Union_League_strength - 4);
    Q.dem_relation -= 2;
!}
go-to: tax_sales

We dispatch a detachment to guard the circuit clerk. He continues his work from the courthouse under military escort and survives the season. The legislator receives no protection. He is shot on the road to a political meeting.

The decision saves one official at the expense of another. Black <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> in the county question why the government could protect the clerk but left their own representative exposed.

@guard_organizers
choose-if: army_strength >= 5 and occupation >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if occupation < 1 : We have no authority to station troops there. ?][? if army_strength < 5 : We have no troops to spare. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_occupation_posture = Math.max(1, Q.FL_occupation_posture || 0);
    Q.FL_garrison_troops = (Q.FL_garrison_troops || 0) + 3;
    Q.army_strength -= 3;
    Q.South_army_strength += 3;
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = Math.max(0, (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) - 4);
    Q.FL_freemen_rep += 3;
    Q.FL_middle_class_rep -= 2;
    Q.Union_League_strength += 4;
    Q.dem_relation -= 2;
!}
go-to: tax_sales

We dispatch a detachment to protect the legislator and his organizers. They continue their political work, and Black voter turnout holds. The circuit clerk, left without a guard, is ambushed near his home and killed.

With his death, the county has no white <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> left in county government. The party retains its Black organizers, but its remaining foothold in the local administration has been destroyed.

@warn_leave
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) + 4;
    Q.FL_freemen_rep -= 4;
    Q.FL_rural_dem += 3;
    Q.Union_League_strength = Math.max(0, Q.Union_League_strength - 6);
    Q.freemen_rep -= 3;
    Q.radical_dissent += 3;
    Q.dem_relation += 2;
!}
go-to: tax_sales

We advise both men to leave the county. They depart, and the killings subside as the Regulators lose their immediate targets. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> organization is left without its leading figures, and those who remain have little reason to believe the government will protect them.

<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> condemn the decision as a surrender. By ordering the threatened officials to abandon their posts, they argue, we have allowed the Regulators to destroy the county's <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> leadership without facing serious resistance.

@tax_sales

The violence has its roots in a dispute over land. Hard times have left many of the county's planters unable to pay their property taxes. <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> officials have responded by selling delinquent land at public tax sales, where freedmen and Northern buyers have purchased farms of their own.

The former owners demand that the sales be halted. The new owners insist that their purchases be honored. The Regulators' campaign has given the dispute a violent edge, with those who enforce the sales and those who benefit from them facing threats of murder.

Florida's <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> leaders are divided over how to proceed. They ask the administration whether the tax sales should continue.

- @continue_sales: Back the tax sales
- @suspend_sales: Quietly suspend the sales

@continue_sales
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_freemen_rep += 3;
    Q.FL_rural_dem += 4;
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) + 5;
    Q.freemen_rep += 2;
    Q.radical_strength += 2;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
!}

We uphold the tax sales. Freedmen retain the land they have purchased, and the state government affirms that delinquent property can be sold under the law.

The decision wins support among Black landowners and strengthens the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> in our party. The planters, however, now have a grievance that reaches beyond the usual contests for office. The Regulators can present their campaign as a struggle to recover land, giving the violence a new source of support.

@suspend_sales
on-arrival: {!
    Q.FL_kkk_strength = Math.max(0, (Q.FL_kkk_strength || 0) - 6);
    Q.FL_freemen_rep -= 4;
    Q.FL_middle_class_dem += 2;
    Q.freemen_rep -= 2;
    Q.radical_dissent += 4;
    Q.dem_relation += 2;
!}

We suspend the tax sales in the hope of restoring order. The planters welcome the decision, and the killings subside. Freedmen who have already purchased land are left uncertain whether their titles will be honored.

<span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> accuse us of yielding to armed intimidation. The government has suspended lawful sales to quiet the men who terrorized the county, leaving Black landowners to bear the cost of the settlement.